PART A. exponent conditions (strict, as g -> 0); minimal integer p_0.
  p_0(g) = (log g^-2)^p_0, R_j ~ (log g_j^-2)^r (r = r_0 of II p. 383).
  (a) R on, II p. 383 prose after (1.78): 2 p_1 - (d+5) r > p_0; if p_1 <= p_0 this gives p_0 > (d+5) r
  (b) R on, (1.88): p_0 > (d+2) r        [linear 2(1+b0)^-1 p_0(g_{j+1}) against R^(d+2)]
  (c) (1.82) base case, R on or R = id (verbatim): 2 p_0 > (d+2) r   [p_0^2 against R^(d+2)]
  (d) R on, (1.95): p_0 > d r             [2 kappa (100 R_k)^d <= p_0(g_k)/4 - 1]
  (e) R = id, merge (1.87) (no extra steps): p_0 > (d+1) r        [linear p_0 against R^(d+1)]
  (f) R = id, base with tail <= x/ln L steps (refined): 2 p_0 > (d+1) r + 1
  CMP 119 (1.1), p. 246: p_0 >= 5 r.   note 49 s5 / note 61 s6a quote 2 p_0 > (d+1) r  [(1.82) has R^(d+2)].

| d | r | (a) p_0 > (d+5)r | (b) p_0 > (d+2)r | (c) 2p_0 > (d+2)r | (d) p_0 > d r | (e) p_0 > (d+1)r | (f) 2p_0 > (d+1)r+1 | p_0 >= 5r ok for (b)? (c)? (e)? |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 3 | 2 | 17 | 11 | 6 | 7 | 9 | 5 | NO / yes / yes (p_0 = 10) |
| 3 | 3 | 25 | 16 | 8 | 10 | 13 | 7 | NO / yes / yes (p_0 = 15) |
| 4 | 2 | 19 | 13 | 7 | 9 | 11 | 6 | NO / yes / NO (p_0 = 10) |
| 4 | 3 | 28 | 19 | 10 | 13 | 16 | 9 | NO / yes / NO (p_0 = 15) |

Binding condition, R on (d = 4): (a) p_0 > 9 r (if p_1 <= p_0), against p_0 >= 5 r of CMP 119 (1.1).
Binding condition, R = id (d = 3): (b)-form p_0 > 5 r verbatim, p_0 > 4 r refined; p_0 >= 5 r meets the refined one.

PART B. L-conditions of the printed geometry (II p. 384-385). L is odd and > 11 in CMP 109 (note 65).
  L_{n-j} <= 42 (1 - L^-(n-j))/(1 - 1/L) < 63 needs 42 L/(L-1) <= 63, i.e. L >= 3;
  L^(-1/2 (n-j)) <= 2^(-(n-j)) needs L >= 4.
| L | 42 L/(L-1) | <= 63 ? | L^(-1/2) | <= 1/2 ? |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2 | 84.00 | NO | 0.7071 | NO |
| 3 | 63.00 | yes | 0.5774 | NO |
| 4 | 56.00 | yes | 0.5000 | yes |
| 5 | 52.50 | yes | 0.4472 | yes |
| 13 | 45.50 | yes | 0.2774 | yes |
| 15 | 45.00 | yes | 0.2582 | yes |

PART C. 3D flow, x_j = x_K + (K-j) ln L; K = 300 steps (all j = 0..K), g^2 = exp(-x_K).
  analytic: (C1) holds once x_j >= 1 (K - j = (x_j - x_K)/ln L < x_j/ln L <= x_j <= x_j^r for L >= 3).
            (C2) needs (x/(x - ln L))^r <= L, i.e. x >= x_b = ln L/(1 - L^(-1/r)).
            (C3) is guaranteed once drops are >= 3 steps apart: x >= x_c = ln L/(1 - L^(-1/(3r))).
| L | r | x_b | x_c | g^2 = e^-x_c |
